{{en-verb}}

# To [[complete]], to bring to [[perfection]], to make [[whole]].
#: {{syn|en|tie in}}
#: {{ux|en|We believe your addition will '''complement''' the team.}}
# To provide what the [[partner]] lacks and [[lack]] what the partner [[provide]]s, thus forming part of a whole.
#: {{ux|en|The flavors of the pepper and garlic '''complement''' each other, giving a very rich taste in combination.}}
#: {{ux|en|I believe our talents really '''complement''' each other.}}
# To change a [[voltage]], [[number]], [[color]], etc. to its complement.

